|money drop = 1,000¢ - 3,950¢
}}

==Enemy==
This wall-type enemy's fast attack rate, high damage, decent range, massive health and singular knockback make Mr. Mer pretty threatening, and if that wasn't enough, his Level 3 [[Mini-Wave]]s can quickly compound your problems by slowly chipping your other units behind, especially when he appears with other threats.

==Strategy==
Mr. Mer's high damage and above-average range means melee units can be outright unusable, and it's optimal to employ [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shields]] that outrange him, or [[:Category:Cats with Wave Immunity|Wave-Immune units]] to dismiss them. Since he is still vulnerable to crowd-control effects, the likes of [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]] and [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]] can be handy. [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Lord of Ruin Jagando Jr.]] is also an effective counter, as he outranges Mr. Mer, while his Strong and Knockback abilities against Traitless mean he can survive for much longer in spite of the Mini-Waves and consistently push Mr. Mer, all while dealing extra damage. When obtained, [[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]] is a particularly great counter to Mr. Mer, being immune to his waves and having Massive damage against him, all on top of outranging him.

